# Per-agent, per-task scratch working directories (_scratch-t5-0337, _scratch-t3-0327, ...). Task
# 0108 decided deliberately that these do NOT travel to the remote. They are a terminal's bench,
# not the runtime: dry-run logs, .err/.sha256 pairs, throwaway psql wrappers, copies of migrations
# already tracked under migrations/. Sixteen of them held 3.5M when this line was written, and
# nothing in the repo reads one -- the only `scratch` the code knows is the brain_scratch DATABASE
# (engine/bin/scratch-db.sh), which is unrelated. Ignored rather than merely left uncommitted so
# the decision survives the next `git add`, on this host and on the VPS clone both.
_scratch-*/

# The staging directory `engine/bin/ledger-store.sh` assembles a capped migration set in. It holds
# COPIES OF FILES ALREADY TRACKED under migrations/, budget/schema/ and queue/schema/, and the
# script removes it on EXIT -- so it is here for the run that was killed, not for the normal one.
# Committing it would put a second, silently ageing copy of the ledger in the tree, which is the
# one thing a schema directory must never contain.
.ledger-store-tmp/

# Runtime working state that is NOT the runtime's source. Two directories, both created by
# systemd units in this repo and both deliberately untracked:
#
#   var/intake/   the intake drop folder. `brain-intake-sweep.timer` runs
#                 `swarm intake --source var/intake` over it every five minutes, and n8n's
#                 push workflow writes into it. Its CONTENTS are inbound messages, some of them
#                 client or personal material that arrived by workflow, so they are exactly the
#                 class of thing that must never reach a remote. The folder is created by
#                 systemd/brain-intake-sweep, so an empty checkout still works.
#   var/state/    watermarks and last-seen markers for the sweeps. Host state, not source: a
#                 second machine cloning this repo must start its own, never inherit this one's.
var/

# 41 ABSOLUTE symlinks into this repo's own migrations/, written by a lane on 2026-08-29 as a
# ledger-42 replica tree. They resolve on the machine that made them and DANGLE IN EVERY CLONE.
# They were deliberately excluded from the record commit and then swept in by a `git add -A` on
# the directory, which is the exact shape this repo forbids. Ignored so it cannot happen a third
# time; the directory itself is kept on disk because the lane's evidence points at it.
outputs/2026-08-29-commander/lane-B6-schema42/
